# tramp_alloc.redefs - the C allocation family, renamed to the trampolines.
#
# Fed to `llvm-objcopy --redefine-syms=` over a DERIVED copy of each pin-built
# library archive under build/lib/<flav>/ (never the pinned archive itself,
# never libc.a / libc++*.a / libunwind.a / libclang_rt.* / cli.o / dsl.o), so
# that every reference the LIBRARY's own objects make to one of these names
# resolves to the tramp_<name> trampoline in tramp_alloc.o (src/tramp_alloc.c),
# which ticks the process-wide allocation-failure schedule once and then
# calls the real function. Applied to every selected archive; the C++ map
# (tramp_alloc_cxx.redefs) is added when `llvm-nm -u` shows an operator-new
# reference. Design: the allocation-failure design, 4.2.
#
# Format: one `old new` pair per line, whitespace-separated; `#` starts a
# comment (both llvm-objcopy and GNU objcopy read this shape). A rename of a
# name the archive does not reference is a no-op, which is why the two names
# the survey found 0 references for (memalign, valloc) are still here: the
# map is the contract, the survey is a measurement.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: free, malloc_usable_size (and operator delete, in the
# C++ map). They allocate nothing, so they have no tick; and the trampolines
# return the REAL allocator's pointer, so the pointer a renamed malloc hands
# the library is exactly the one an unrenamed free expects -- pairing needs no
# counterpart. Also absent: pvalloc (musl has none) and libc-internal callers
# of these names (fopen, getdelim, regcomp, strdup's own malloc): they are in
# libc.a, which is never renamed, and a NULL there would be "a counterexample
# that refutes nothing" (faultalloc.h).
malloc tramp_malloc
calloc tramp_calloc
realloc tramp_realloc
reallocarray tramp_reallocarray
aligned_alloc tramp_aligned_alloc
posix_memalign tramp_posix_memalign
memalign tramp_memalign
valloc tramp_valloc
strdup tramp_strdup
strndup tramp_strndup
